// BT-3872 (ADR 0132 Phase 1d): an open `Value subclass:`. An open
// method's self-send is late-bound (a subclass may override it), so its pass-on
// stays a plain send; a `sealed` method's binds to this module's entry. A use of
// `a` that holds a use of `b` (`both:with:`) threads neither and compiles as a
// plain method. Read by threaded_value_entry_test.bt.

Value subclass: ThreadedOpenValueFixture

  twice: b =>
    b value
    b value

  sealed sealedTwice: b =>
    b value
    b value

  viaOpen: b => self twice: b

  viaSealed: b => self sealedTwice: b

  apply: f to: x => f value: x

  both: a with: b => self apply: a to: (b value)
